{"id": "section-body-21894", "title": "Chronic Pulmonary Embolism", "chapterId": "chapter-twenty", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "CARDIOVASCULAR DISEASE CONDITIONS", "Pulmonary Embolism", "Chronic Pulmonary Embolism"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-21894", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Chronic Pulmonary Embolism", "runs": [{"text": "Chronic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Pulmonary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Embolism"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "781"}}, {"id": "body-21895", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Chronic pulmonary embolism is mainly a consequence of incomplete resolution of acute pulmonary thromboembolism. Clinically symptoms and signs may be preceded by Acute Pulmonary Embolism for more than 2weeks.", "runs": [{"text": "Chronic pulmonary embolism is mainly a consequence of incomplete resolution of acute pulmonary thromboembolism. Clinically "}, {"text": "symptoms and signs may be preceded by Acute Pulmonary Embolism for more than 2weeks."}]}, {"id": "body-21897", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-21898", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Long-term oral anticoagulation", "runs": [{"text": "Long-term"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "oral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "anticoagulation"}]}, {"id": "body-21900", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "C: warfarin (PO) 2–10mg 24hourly", "runs": [{"text": "C:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "warfarin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2–10mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "24hourly"}]}, {"id": "body-21901", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "(Maintain INR 2.0–3.0 for warfarin use individuals.)", "runs": [{"text": "(Maintain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "INR"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2.0–3.0"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "warfarin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "use"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "individuals.)"}]}, {"id": "body-21902", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-21903", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "S: rivaroxaban (PO) 15-20mg 24hourly", "runs": [{"text": "S:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "rivaroxaban"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "15-20mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "24hourly"}]}, {"id": "body-21905", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Referral: All cases suspected of pulmonary embolism should be referred to a high level of care", "runs": [{"text": "Referral:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "All"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cases"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "suspected"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pulmonary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "embolism"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "referred"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "high"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "level"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "care"}]}, {"id": "body-21906", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "IVC filter (IVC filters are a valuable tool for preventing PE in patients who cannot be managed with anticoagulation, but their use should be carefully considered due to the increased risk of DVT and potential long-term complications. Their benefit is most pronounced in the early period after placement, and filters should be removed when no longer indicated", "runs": [{"text": "IVC filter (IVC filters are a valuable tool for preventing PE in patients who cannot be managed with anticoagulation, but their use"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "